# oracle: bond_style bpm/rotational with zero critical values fcr fcs tct tcb = 0 (native BondBPMRotational::coeff has no range check). Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the bond is not broken at a stretch of 1.0 (energy 0.25, as with 1000), while a small positive value of 0.05 breaks it (energy 0 after the same stretch).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-12
units lj
atom_style bpm/sphere
atom_modify map yes
comm_modify vel yes cutoff 3.0
newton off
region box block -5 5 -5 5 -5 5
create_box 1 box bond/types 1 extra/bond/per/atom 1
create_atoms 1 single 0 0 0
create_atoms 1 single 1.2 0 0
set atom * diameter 1.0
set atom * mass 1.0
create_bonds single/bond 1 1 2
bond_style bpm/rotational smooth no break yes
bond_coeff 1 1.0 1.0 1.0 1.0 0 0 0 0 0.1 0.1 0.1 0.1
pair_style zero 1.0
pair_coeff * *
special_bonds lj 0.0 1.0 1.0 coul 1.0 1.0 1.0
neighbor 0.3 bin
fix 1 all nve/bpm/sphere
thermo_style custom step pe ebond
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run 0
set atom 2 x 2.2
run 0
set atom 2 x 3.5
run 0
set atom 2 x 1.0
run 0
